module bindings.rust.type_erasure_missing_lifetime_bound;

// A function erases one of its own generic parameters behind an untyped raw
// pointer -- `Arc::into_raw(wake) as *const ()` -- while no type parameter it
// declares carries a lifetime bound.
//
// A raw pointer keeps no trace of the lifetime of what it points at, and the
// untyped spelling drops the type as well, so whatever receives the pointer --
// a raw vtable, a struct field, a return value -- can restore the type and
// call into it after the original value is gone. That is use after free, and
// the borrow checker cannot object, because the pointer type carries nothing
// to check. The signature is the only place left to state the constraint, so
// the erasure is only checkable when the erased parameter carries a lifetime
// bound ('static or a named lifetime).
//
// Only parameters the function declares itself count: a method whose receiver
// type comes from the surrounding impl carries its obligation there, and a
// non-generic function erases a concrete type with no lifetime to lose. The
// fact is emitted by the frontend from the syntax tree, so comments and prose
// cannot satisfy or defeat it.
binding typeErasureMissingLifetimeBound {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.kind == "any" and node.analysis == "rust.type_erasure_missing_lifetime_bound"
  emit issue code.TypeErasureMissingLifetimeBound at node
}
